Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Alan Ruttenberg")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Alexander D. Diehl")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Alexander P. Cox")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Bill Duncan")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Kinga Szigeti")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Marcus Ng")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Mark Jensen")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Naveed Chaudhry")
Annotation(dcterms:contributor "Patrick L. Ray")
Annotation(dcterms:description "The Neurological Disease Ontology (ND) provides a set of logically connected classes that represent the range of neurological diseases and their associated signs and symptoms, assessments, diagnoses, and interventions encountered in the course of clinical practice. ND is built as an extension of the Ontology for General Medical Sciences (OGMS). Classes in ND utilize both textual and axiomatized definitions that describe and formalize the relations between classes within the ontology itself as well as to classes in external ontologies.")
Annotation(dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>)
Annotation(dcterms:title "Neurological Disease Ontology")
Annotation(rdfs:comment "More information can be found at https://github.com/addiehl/neurological-disease-ontology

There is a google group for discussing the ND project found at https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl=en&fromgroups#!forum/nd-ontology

If you are interested in participating in the development of ND, please send an email to addiehl_at_buffalo.edu."@en)

