# Class: obo:ND_0001073 (diagnosis of transverse myelitis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001073 "inflammation of a transverse portion of the spinal cord characterized by acute or subacute segmental demyelination or necrosis. The condition may occur sporadically, follow an infection or vaccination, or present as a paraneoplastic syndrome (see also ENCEPHALOMYELITIS, ACUTE DISSEMINATED). Clinical manifestations include motor weakness, sensory loss, and incontinence (MeSH).
")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001073 "Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0001073 "http://neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Transverse_Myelitis")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000232 obo:ND_0001073 "Change entity URI")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:ND_0001073 "birnlex_12520")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001073 "diagnosis of transverse myelitis")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001073 obo:ND_0001066)

# Class: obo:ND_0001100 (diagnostic guideline)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001100 "A directive information entity that specifies how to establish a diagnosis according to one or more clinical findings, the concretization of which is realized in a diagnostic process.

Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001100 "A directive information entity the concretization of which is realized in a diagnostic process and which has a set of diagnostic criteria that consist of clinical findings that have been agreed upon by the medical community to provide sufficient, necessary, or sufficient and necessary warrant for a clinician to reach a particular diagnosis concerning a patient whose clinical picture satisfies the relevant diagnostic criteria.  A diagnostic guideline has as parts the objective of accurately diagnosing patients according to its diagnostic criteria and the directive for the clinician to make the associated diagnosis when the diagnostic criteria have been determined to be satisfied.

Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001100 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000232 obo:ND_0001100 "This class belongs in the domain of OGMS, will be a subtype of IAO_0000033:'directive information entity'. Refer to:

http://code.google.com/p/ogms/wiki/DiagnosisGuideline

http://code.google.com/p/ogms/issues/detail?id=75

https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!topic/ogms-discuss/9oVK5dLdZQs")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001100 "diagnostic guideline")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001100 obo:IAO_0000033)

# Class: obo:ND_0001101 (diagnostic guideline for mild cognitive impairment)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001101 "*** REVISE ***

Cognitive impairments beyond those expected based on the age and education of the individual, but which are not significant enough to interfere with their daily activities.

The diagnosis of MCI requires considerable clinical judgement as well as a comprehensive clinical assessment including clinical observation, neuroimaging, blood tests and neuropsychological testing in order to rule out an alternate diagnosis.

MCI is diagnosed when there is:

1. Evidence of memory impairment
2. Preservation of general cognitive and functional abilities
3. Absence of diagnosed dementia")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001101 "Memory complaint, preferably corroborated by an informant
Objective memory impairment (below 1.5 standard deviations)
Normal general cognitive functioning
Intact activities of daily living
Not demented")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001101 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0001101 "Adapted from: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mild_cognitive_impairment")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0001101 "http://www.mejfm.com/journal/Oct2004/Dementia.htm")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001101 "diagnostic guideline for mild cognitive impairment")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001101 obo:ND_0001100)

# Class: obo:ND_0001102 (diagnostic guideline for dementia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001102 "*** REVISE ***

A diagnosis of dementia in a patient based on findings from blood tests, neuroimaging, and cognitive testing that indicate the presence of cognitive deficits [visual spatial, attention, orientation, exceutive function, functional] severe enough to interfere with the patient's daily life in a previously unimpaired person.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001102 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001102 "diagnostic guideline for dementia")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001102 obo:ND_0001101)

# Class: obo:ND_0001103 (diagnostic guideline for infectious dementia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001103 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001103 "diagnostic guideline for infectious dementia")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001103 obo:ND_0001102)

# Class: obo:ND_0001104 (diagnostic guideline for vascular dementia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0001104 "A. The development of multiple cognitive deficits manifested by both:

Memory impairment (impaired ability to learn new information or to recall previously learned information)
One or more of the following cognitive disturbances:
(a) aphasia (language disturbance)

(b) apraxia (impaired ability to carry out motor activities depite intact motor function)

(c) agnosia (failure to recognize or identify objects despite intact sensory function)

(d) disturbance in executive functioning (i.e., planning, organizing, sequencing, abstracting)
B. The cognitive deficits in criteria A1 and A2 each cause significant impairment in social or occupational functioning and represent a significant decline from a previous level of functioning.

C. Focal neurological signs and symptoms (e.g., exggeration of deep tendon reflexes, extensor plantar response, psuedobulbar palsy, gait abnormalities, weakness of an extremity) or laboratory evidence indicative of cerebrovascular disease (e.g., multiple infarctions involving cortex and underlyig white matter) that are judged to be etiologically related to the disturbance.

D. The deficits do not ocurr exclusively during the course of a delirium.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0001104 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0001104 "http://www.strokecenter.org/professionals/stroke-diagnosis/stroke-assessment-scales/dsm-iv-criteria-for-the-diagnosis-of-vascular-dementia/")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0001104 "diagnostic guideline for vascular dementia")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0001104 obo:ND_0001102)

