# Class: obo:ND_0003000 (dementia)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003000 "Dementia is the co-occurence of cognitive deficits in at least two domains [memory, visual spatial, attention, orientation, executive function, functional] resulting in a decline of previous functioning.  It typically results from the realization of a dementia disease.

*** TEMPLATE FOR SYNDROME DEFINITIONS??? ***")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:ND_0003000 "I think this is incorrect. First it should be defined wrt its parent. I don't think the parent of \"dementia syndrome\" will turn out to be \"MCI syndrome\". Admittedly that will depend on the specifics to the aggreed upon definitions. Currently they are both in need or refinement.
Second, the definition is too Alzheimer-centric, and I believe would rule out other instances of dementia. Dementia does not typically result from a \"dementia disease\". Even if true, whatever “typical” means, that assertion is informative, not explanatory — i.e., it belongs in an elucidation not the definition.  

Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003000 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003000 "Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003000 "dementia")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003000 obo:ND_0003004)

# Class: obo:ND_0003001 (Parkinsonism)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003001 "Parkinsonism is the co-occurence of any combination of the classical features of Parkinson's disease [tremor, rigidity, akinesia/bradykinesia, postural instability].  It typically results from the realization of either Parkinsons disease, progressive supranuclear palsy, or multiple system atrophy.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003001 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003001 "Parkinsonian syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003001 "idiopathic parkinsonism")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003001 "Parkinsonism")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003001 obo:OGMS_0000086)

# Class: obo:ND_0003002 (typical Alzheimers syndrome)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003002 "Typical Alzheimers syndrome is the insidious onset of dementia syndrome that is characterized by episodic memory loss.  It typically results from the realization of Alzheimers disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003002 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003002 "typical Alzheimers syndrome")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003002 obo:ND_0003000)

# Class: obo:ND_0003003 (Parkinson plus syndrome)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003003 "Parkinson plus syndrome is the co-occurence of any combination of the classical features of Parkinsons disease [tremor, rigidity, akinesia/bradykinesia, postural instability] with additional features [supranuclear palsy, paralysis of downward gaze, autonomic dysfunction, additional cortical signs, etc] that distinguishes it from simple idiopathic Parkinsons disease.  It typically results from the realization of either multiple system atrophy, progressive supranuclear palsy, corticobasal degeneration, or Lewy body dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003003 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003003 "atypical parkinsonian")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003003 "disorder of multiple system degeneration")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003003 "Parkinson plus syndrome")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003003 obo:ND_0003001)

# Class: obo:ND_0003004 (mild cognitive impairment)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003004 "Mild cognitive impairment is the occurence of one or more cognitive deficits [visual spatial, attention, orientation, executive function, functional] that are beyond those expected based on the age and education of the individual, but which are not significant enough to interfere with their daily activities.  It is typically the result of _________ .")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:ND_0003004 "Remove last sentence of defintion. \"Typically\" doesn't ontologize well. Nor do fill-in-the-blanks ;-)

Mark Jensen
")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:ND_0003004 "Suggest removing 'mild' from label. Dementia is not a type of mild cognitive impairment. A syndrome of cognitive impairment makes more sense and tracks far better with reality. 

A diagnosis of MCI can be non-pathological, ie- normal ageing related cognitive decline.

Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003004 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003004 "Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003004 "MCI")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000232 obo:ND_0003004 obo:IAO_0000428)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003004 "mild cognitive impairment")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003004 obo:OGMS_0000086)

# Class: obo:ND_0003005 (atypical Alzheimers syndrome)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003005 "Atypical Alzheimers syndrome is the insidious onset of dementia syndrome that is typically characterized by the absence of episodic memory loss.  It typically results from the realization of either frontal variant of Alzheimers disease, logopenic aphasia, posterior cortical atrophy, or primary progressive nonfluent aphasia.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003005 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003005 "atypical Alzheimers syndrome")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003005 obo:ND_0003000)

# Class: obo:ND_0003006 (epilepsy)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003006 "Epilepsy is the occurence of multiple seizures over the course of an individual's life.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003006 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003006 "epilepsy")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003006 obo:OGMS_0000086)

# Class: obo:ND_0003007 (sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003007 "ALS without family history")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003007 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003007 "sporadic ALS")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0003007 "See: http://www.alshopefoundation.org/understanding-als/types-of-als.php")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003007 "sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003007 obo:ND_0000120)

# Class: obo:ND_0003008 (familial amyotrophic lateral sclerosis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003008 "Familial ALS cases comprise 5 to 10 percent of all cases of ALS. Familial ALS (FALS) is inherited as an autosomal dominant trait. Almost 20 % of people with FALS have damage (called a mutation) in the gene that codes for the protein Cu/Zn superoxide dismutase (SOD 1) located on chromosome 21. There are no differences between familial and sporadic ALS on neurological exam except for occasional sensory loss in people with FALS. Other genes that, when damaged, can lead to ALS, have been identified on chromosomes 2, 9, 15, 18 and the X chromosome.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003008 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003008 "familial ALS")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0003008 "See: http://www.alshopefoundation.org/understanding-als/types-of-als.php")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003008 "familial amyotrophic lateral sclerosis")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003008 obo:ND_0000120)

# Class: obo:ND_0003009 (western pacific amyotrophic lateral sclerosis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003009 "Western Pacific ALS occurs primarily on the island of Guam, the Kii Peninsula of Japan, and New Guinea. The people on Guam have the same clinical characteristics seen in sporadic ALS and also can have a dementia and Parkinsons like illness. The illness on Guam is the first to be tied to a toxin, the cycad nut. This nut contains a compound that is toxic to nerve cells called BMAA and is similar to glutamate. The nut is eaten by the fruit bat which was a delicacy among the Chamorro population of Guam. This allowed a very high concentration of the toxin to be eaten and it has been postulated but not proven, that this caused the disease. The fruit bat was eaten to extinction and now fruit bats for consumption are imported, the disease has all but disappeared!")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003009 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003009 "Guamanian")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003009 "western pacific ALS")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0003009 "See: http://www.alshopefoundation.org/understanding-als/types-of-als.php")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003009 "western pacific amyotrophic lateral sclerosis")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003009 obo:ND_0000120)

# Class: obo:ND_0003010 (juvenile amyotrophic lateral sclerosis)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003010 "Rare cases of adolescent motor neuron disease that are clinically indistinguishable from ALS have been reported. Onset is between ages twelve and sixteen. Although ALS can occur at young ages, these cases are probably different from sporadic ALS.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003010 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0003010 "juvenile ALS")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0003010 "See: http://www.alshopefoundation.org/understanding-als/types-of-als.php")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003010 "juvenile amyotrophic lateral sclerosis")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003010 obo:ND_0000120)

# Class: obo:ND_0003011 (hiramaya disease)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0003011 "This is a rare disorder seem in young men. In this variant there is localized atrophy of one arm associated with increased reflexes implicating the presence of upper and lower motor neuron damage. However, the disorder is a problem at the junction between the cervical spine and the skull where there is pressure on the cervical spinal cord. In order to detect it, MRI of the neck needs to be performed in different positions including neck flexion and extension.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0003011 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0003011 "See: http://www.alshopefoundation.org/understanding-als/types-of-als.php")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0003011 "hiramaya disease")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0003011 obo:ND_0000120)

