# Class: obo:ND_0006016 (dysmyelination)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0006016 "A pathological process that results in abnormal growth or maintence of white matter in an organism's brain.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0006016 "Mark Jensen")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:ND_0006016 "A generic term that will probably be replaced by the more correct term leukodystrophy, that is used for a variety of congenital white matter diseases in which myelin is never formed correctly or is not maintained due to some sort of enzymatic defect.

From:
http://www.medcyclopaedia.com/library/topics/volume_vi_1/d/dysmyelinating_diseases.aspx")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:ND_0006016 "The leukodystrophies are caused by imperfect growth or development of the myelin sheath, the fatty covering that acts as an insulator around nerve fibers. Myelin, from which the white matter of the brain takes its colour, is a complex substance made up of at least ten different chemicals. Each of the leukodystrophies is the result of a defect in the gene that controls the production or metabolism of one (and only one) of the component molecules of myelin. [Wikipedia]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0006016 "dysmyelination")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0006016 obo:OGMS_0000061)

# Class: obo:ND_0006017 (autoimmune process)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0006017 "A specific humoral or cell-mediated immune response against autologous (self) antigens. An autoimmune process may produce or be caused by autoimmune disease and may be developmentally complex, not necessarily pathological, and possibly pervasive.")
