# Class: obo:ND_0008018 (intracerebral hemorrhage)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0008018 "an Intracerebral hemorrhage is a hemmorhagic stroke with physical basis in the brain is caused by high blood pressure, trauma,vascular malformations and is the result of a blood vessel in the brain bursting and spilling over into the brain and results in brain cell damage and infaraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008018 "Donat Sule")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008018 "Marcus Ng")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008018 "Naveed Chaudhry")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0008018 "http://www.mayoclinic.com/health/stroke/DS00150/DSECTION=causes")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:ND_0008018 "Intracerebral hemorrhage. In an intracerebral hemorrhage, a blood vessel in the brain bursts and spills into the surrounding brain tissue, damaging brain cells. Brain cells beyond the leak are deprived of blood and damaged. High blood pressure, trauma, vascular malformations, use of blood-thinning medications and other conditions may cause intracerebral hemorrhage. ")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0008018 "intracerebral hemorrhage")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0008018 obo:ND_0008003)

# Class: obo:ND_0008020 (subarachnoid hemorrhage)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:ND_0008020 "A subarachnoid hemorrage is a hemorrhagic stroke that has physical basis on the surface of the brain and is caused by the rupture of an aneurysm and is the result of an artery on the surface of your brain bursting and spilling into the pia mater which is often charchterized by a sudden thunderclap headache and results in brain cell damage and infaraction. (may lead to vasospasm which may cause further cell damage via ischema)")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008020 "Donat Sule")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008020 "Marcus Ng")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008020 "Naveed Chaudhry")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:ND_0008020 "Subarachnoid hemorrhage. In a subarachnoid hemorrhage, an artery on or near the surface of your brain bursts and spills into the space between the surface of your brain and your skull. This bleeding is often signaled by a sudden, severe headache. A subarachnoid hemorrhage is commonly caused by the rupture of an aneurysm, a small sack-shaped or berry-shaped outpouching on an artery in the brain. After the hemorrhage, the blood vessels in your brain may widen and narrow erratically (vasospasm), causing brain cell damage by further limiting blood flow to parts of your brain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 " from Ropper/Brown; Pinciples of Neurology. 8th ed- look over") obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0008020 "ruptured saccular aneurysm")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 " from Ropper/Brown; Pinciples of Neurology. 8th ed- look over") obo:IAO_0000118 obo:ND_0008020 "spontaneous subarachnoid hemorrhage")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:ND_0008020 "http://www.mayoclinic.com/health/stroke/DS00150/DSECTION=causes")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:ND_0008020 "subarachnoid hemorrhage")
SubClassOf(obo:ND_0008020 obo:ND_0008003)

# Class: obo:ND_0008021 (primary intracerebral hemorrhage)

