# Class: obo:OGMS_0000045 (obo:OGMS_0000045)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:OGMS_0000045 "Alexander P. Cox")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:OGMS_0000045 "**** NOTE ****

To assert that something is clinically abnormal is then to state:

(1) that it is not part of the life plan for an organism of the relevant type (thus aging or pregnancy are not clinically abnormal),
(2) that it is causally linked to an elevated risk of pain or suffering or other feelings of illness or of death or dysfunction on the part of the organism, and
(3) that it is such that this elevated risk exceeds a certain threshold level.

From pages 8-9 of Ceusters and Smith \"Foundations for a realist ontology of mental disease\", Journal of Biomedical Semantics 2010, 1:10 http://www.jbiomedsem.com/content/1/1/10

Alexander P. Cox")
SubClassOf(obo:OGMS_0000045 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000127 obo:OGMS_0000031))
SubClassOf(obo:OGMS_0000045 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000171 obo:OGMS_0000087))
DisjointClasses(obo:OGMS_0000045 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ND#normal>)

# Class: obo:OGMS_0000063 (obo:OGMS_0000063)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:OGMS_0000063 "Why isn't 'disease course' a subclass of 'bodily process'?  There is currently no definition for 'bodily process', but perhaps it is intended to capture only those processes that occur in the body that are \"normal\" or \"non-diseased\".  If this is the intended distinction, it will undoubtedly be very difficult to construct an acceptable definition that will even hold up in most cases.

APC")
SubClassOf(obo:OGMS_0000063 ObjectIntersectionOf(ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:OGMS_0000031) ObjectAllValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000055 obo:OGMS_0000031)))
SubClassOf(obo:OGMS_0000063 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000057 obo:OGMS_0000087))

# Class: obo:OGMS_0000073 (obo:OGMS_0000073)

SubClassOf(obo:OGMS_0000073 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ND#is_about> ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:OBI_0100026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000087 obo:OBI_0000093) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000158 obo:OGMS_0000031))))

# Class: obo:OGMS_0000086 (obo:OGMS_0000086)

DisjointClasses(obo:OGMS_0000086 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ND#normal>)

